  "body": "## Summary\n- turn the existing React frontend into an installable phone-first PWA while preserving the complete desktop feature set\n- add polished mobile navigation covering the current Dashboard, Runtime, Bots, offers, history, pricing and dictionary workflows\n- add a dedicated CAPTCHA queue and remote manual browser viewer\n- keep the browser and bot session on the PC; the phone only relays the user's direct pointer/touch gesture to the active headed Playwright page\n- add a loopback-only Playwright control bridge and a Spring proxy so the Playwright `Page` is never accessed from arbitrary HTTP threads\n- preserve the existing `bot-X.json` recovery/save/resume lifecycle\n\n## Manual CAPTCHA flow\n`CAPTCHA_REQUIRED -> phone CAPTCHA queue -> start recovery -> PC opens headed browser with the same session -> real challenge becomes visible -> phone receives current browser frames -> user's DOWN/MOVE/UP gesture is queued -> owning Playwright thread applies it -> verification clears -> session is saved -> bot resumes headless`\n\nThe remote control deliberately does not choose or synthesize a CAPTCHA solution. It maps the user's actual gesture onto the browser viewport.\n\n## Connectivity\nThe app continues to use relative `/api` routes. Remote phone access is intended through a private network such as Tailscale rather than exposing the Playwright bridge publicly; the Playwright bridge itself only binds to loopback.",
